{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 5291332,
  "courseSlug": "chatgpt-bard-bing-complete-guide-to-chatgpt-openai-apis",
  "courseTitle": "ChatGPT & Generative AI - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37885396",
      "title": "Creating Custom Options / Custom Parameters with /prefer",
      "sourceHash": "7e93cbf681d032a8b28e56cb1c599076ba0de69e51139d4580aaa84c78da9d02",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "So parameters are great,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "but adding these again and again is a bit cumbersome,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "especially as you probably have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.66,
          "en": "some specific image styles in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.66,
          "end": 15,
          "en": "which you use quite frequently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "So you often have a specific parameter combination you use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 21.69,
          "en": "for specific images you want to create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.69,
          "end": 23.13,
          "en": "To make this a bit easier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.13,
          "end": 27.63,
          "en": "we can create parameter templates, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.63,
          "end": 29.523,
          "en": "or custom parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 32.88,
          "en": "To access this option, we have to enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.88,
          "end": 34.413,
          "en": "the preferred command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 37.83,
          "en": "There, we have plenty of commands available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.83,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "The only ones we need now is prefer option set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 42.633,
          "en": "and prefer option list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.89,
          "end": 45.63,
          "en": "Prefer option list will list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.63,
          "end": 48.3,
          "en": "all your current custom options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.3,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "Typically, you won't have any",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "if you didn't ever use this option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "And with prefer option set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 58.85,
          "en": "we can create new custom options, new custom parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "So with TAB, we access the option field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 63.96,
          "en": "The option field here simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.96,
          "end": 67.41,
          "en": "what should this custom parameter be named.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.41,
          "end": 70.65,
          "en": "You can give these parameters any name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.65,
          "end": 74.7,
          "en": "only names of already existing parameters cannot be chosen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.7,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "So for example, the style parameter which we use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 80.61,
          "en": "to apply the raw style, is taken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.61,
          "end": 83.01,
          "en": "Same thing applies to things like AR,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.01,
          "end": 86.82,
          "en": "so anything you can refer to with this double dash command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.82,
          "end": 91.82,
          "en": "but here we could call this perimeter raw image for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "As said, you can give this a more creative name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 96.15,
          "en": "if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "Don't add enter now by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 100.02000000000001,
          "en": "because this will delete the parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.02000000000001,
          "end": 103.59,
          "en": "with this given name, instead hit TAB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.59,
          "end": 105.69,
          "en": "And there you can select the value field now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.69,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "as a second option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 111,
          "en": "This now defines the parameters that you will apply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 114.993,
          "en": "when using this custom parameter in your prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.07,
          "end": 118.38,
          "en": "There we could, for example, say that we wanna set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.38,
          "end": 120.27,
          "en": "the style perimeter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.27,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "Here, we again have to refer to this perimeter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 125.82,
          "en": "with the double dashes to raw,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.82,
          "end": 130.083,
          "en": "and that the aspect ratio should be set to 16.9.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.25,
          "end": 135.66,
          "en": "Now with ENTER, we created this custom parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.66,
          "end": 140.66,
          "en": "this custom option, and with preferred option list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.03,
          "end": 146.03,
          "en": "and ENTER, we can now see the name of this custom parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 148.62,
          "en": "and the parameters that are stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.62,
          "end": 150.363,
          "en": "in this custom option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 155.973,
          "en": "So if we now create a new image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 161.603,
          "en": "let's say photo of four people playing soccer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 164.823,
          "en": "to keep things simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.26,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "Now, just as we added the normal parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "we can now add our double dashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 177.633,
          "en": "and refer to our raw image perimeter that we created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.92000000000002,
          "end": 183.92,
          "en": "With ENTER, we now automatically add the stored parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.04,
          "end": 187.5,
          "en": "inside our custom parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.5,
          "end": 189.993,
          "en": "to the prompt of our image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "So this is nice to know and definitely helpful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 198.54,
          "en": "but actually this is even more powerful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.54,
          "end": 201.36,
          "en": "because you cannot only store parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.36,
          "end": 204.12,
          "en": "inside your custom parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 208.413,
          "en": "you can also store normal text prompts in this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.64,
          "end": 212.01,
          "en": "Let me give you an example for this now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.01,
          "end": 215.163,
          "en": "So we again, open our options set menu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.36,
          "end": 218.52,
          "en": "and now I could store my entire options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.52,
          "end": 222.3,
          "en": "for a specific setting inside my parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.3,
          "end": 224.853,
          "en": "my custom parameter that I can create here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.02,
          "end": 230.49,
          "en": "So if I call this Simpson's selfie for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.49,
          "end": 233.55,
          "en": "to be very creative again with the naming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.55,
          "end": 234.993,
          "en": "and now adding a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.18,
          "end": 239.91,
          "en": "where we don't add any double dashes now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 242.1,
          "en": "because we won't store a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 245.79,
          "en": "but instead say that we want to have a selfie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.79,
          "end": 247.353,
          "en": "in Simpson's style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 252.6,
          "en": "With ENTER, we save this custom option now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.6,
          "end": 257.6,
          "en": "and then by creating a comic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.02,
          "end": 261.78,
          "en": "of a family sitting on the couch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.78,
          "end": 266.14,
          "en": "and now I simply add --simpsons-selfie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.2,
          "end": 272.52,
          "en": "and as we saw it above,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.52,
          "end": 277.35,
          "en": "we now added these text prompts that we stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.35,
          "end": 282.243,
          "en": "inside our Simpson's selfie custom parameter to our prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 283.26,
          "end": 284.90999999999997,
          "en": "And if we check the results,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 284.90999999999997,
          "end": 287.19,
          "en": "then well these are not perfect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 289.44,
          "en": "but definitely we have selfies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 293.52,
          "en": "and we actually also have this one and that one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 295.56,
          "en": "in Simpson's style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 295.56,
          "end": 297.65999999999997,
          "en": "We should probably further tailor this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.65999999999997,
          "end": 299.73,
          "en": "because I see many, many glitches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 299.73,
          "end": 301.53,
          "en": "and errors in these images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.53,
          "end": 304.32,
          "en": "but the core idea of saving information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 304.32,
          "end": 306.03,
          "en": "inside a custom parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 306.03,
          "end": 308.793,
          "en": "became quite obvious in this example, I guess.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ],
      "lectureOrder": 185,
      "videoOrder": 185
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
